    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule following the existing `namesakeCount` pattern (a derived value stored on the `Owner` at create time and consumed by the MapStruct mapper).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after computing the household members, set the household size on the new owner to `householdMembers.size() + 1` (existing members plus the one being created), capturing the \"after this create\" size.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 extended the `membershipTier` expression so it returns `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER (namesakeCount == 0 and non-blank email) / BRONZE rules.\n\n4. **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `household_size` column to the `owners` table so persistence works across all supported databases (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` \u2014 which builds a 3-member shared household and asserts the third member is GOLD \u2014 passes, and the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic is preserved as the fallback.",
